  "equipment_type": "Sensor (ultrasonic flowmeter)",
  "applies_to": "UFC 400 signal converter with Modbus, electronic revision ER 2.2.0_, Modbus version 2.1.0_, supplementary instructions 4002744801 R01 (05/2013).",
  "summary": "The UFC 400 is KROHNE's signal converter for ultrasonic flowmeters. With the Modbus option it is an RS-485 Modbus RTU slave. This map covers flow velocity, volume and mass flow, sound velocity, gain and SNR (overall and per path), NAMUR NE 107 status bytes, the totalisers, process input parameters, serial settings and the control coils.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The manual lists protocol addresses that go into the request unchanged: input register 30006 is requested as 30006 (0x7536); each row also prints the hex value. Register numbers, if a tool wants them, are the address + 1."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "ER 2.2.0_ / Modbus 2.1.0_",
  "source": {
    "title": "UFC 400 Supplementary instructions - Signal converter for ultrasonic flowmeters - Description of Modbus interface",
    "doc_number": "4002744801 R01",
    "revision_date": "2013-05",
    "url": "https://core.instrumart.com/assets/Krohne-UFC-400-Modbus-Manual.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "Serial defaults p. 7; addressing p. 8; data representation pp. 9-10; address ranges p. 11; parameter tables pp. 14-22"
  },
  "notes": [
    "This is an unaltered copy of the KROHNE document hosted by distributor Instrumart; no public KROHNE URL for this revision was found in the time available.",
    "Data representation (pp. 9-10): 16-bit values are MSB first; 32- and 64-bit values follow the 'Register Format' setting (holding 50006). Big Endian, the default, puts the most significant word in the first register (ABCD); the manual's Little Endian diagram keeps bytes in order inside each register but reverses the registers (CDAB).",
    "Holding registers are written with function 16 (0x10). Configuration changes take effect only after 'Apply Changes' (coil 1002).",
    "Totaliser 3 registers are footnoted in the manual as available only on signal converters with the 'modular carrier'.",
    "Left out: NE 107 status groups (39004, Long), diagnostics selectors 41002/41003 (long code lists), NE 107 event-group signal registers 52000+, and device identification via function 43.",
    "Byte-type parameters each occupy one register and are listed as UINT16.",
    "Left out: transmission delay 50002 (Float), because the table gives its unit as ms while the range is printed as 0...0.04."
  ],
